From: Cristodcgomez <cristo.c.mc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bt: btpower: tolerate the -EINVAL from regulator_set_voltage

On monaco the BT rails (qcom,bt-vdd-io/core/pa/xtal) are FIXED RPM regulators
(min==max), but btpower asks for a range (e.g. 3000000-3312000 for PA) and the
core returns -EINVAL even though the target value is the one the rail already
has. btpower aborts bluetooth_power(1) -> the chip is not powered and btattach
hangs (no reset, but no HCI). Do not abort: log and continue with the enable.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [dace bring-up]
Signed-off-by: Cristodcgomez <cristo.c.mc@gmail.com>
---

--- a/private/msm-google-modules/bt/pwr/btpower.c
+++ b/private/msm-google-modules/bt/pwr/btpower.c
@@ -292,9 +292,14 @@
 						vreg->min_vol,
 						vreg->max_vol);
 			if (rc < 0) {
-				pr_err("%s: regulator_set_voltage(%s) failed rc=%d\n",
+				/* dace: on monaco the BT rails are FIXED RPM
+				 * regulators (min==max) and the core rejects
+				 * the range with -EINVAL even though the value is
+				 * the correct one. Do not abort; the rail is already
+				 * at its voltage, continue with the enable. */
+				pr_warn("%s: set_voltage(%s) rc=%d (fixed rail, ignored)\n",
 						__func__, vreg->name, rc);
-				goto out;
+				rc = 0;
 			}
 		}
 
